{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_document", "label": "Implementation Plan: WorkflowHub Complexity Governance", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L1-1337", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_material_revision_module", "label": "MaterialRevision Data Model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L141-147, L176", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single current revision of the four materials plus requirements ledger/coverage records parent_ref/hash, the four material refs and hashes, changed files and source, and is create-only with CAS. It must not decide tests, review or formal completion."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_quality_fact_module", "label": "QualityFact Data Model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L148-154, L177", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Appends test, AC, review, confirmation and authorization facts as create-only records carrying kind, subject task/stage/tree/material, result and source tool/provider, and derives freshness against current identity. It must not decide whether materials may continue to be edited."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_publication_module", "label": "Publication Module", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L155-161, L178", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Consumes the current revision/tree plus fresh quality facts and atomically publishes per-stage complete/incomplete/fail-loud results (stage, current identity, satisfied, missing, status); the view is rebuildable and must not decide irreversible Git operation permissions."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_deletion_proof_module", "label": "DeletionProof Contract", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L179", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fields are consumer, quality_semantic, replacement, before_after_oracle, fault_injection, Multica, legacy, rollback and user_decision, held as ordinary plan/evidence fields with no lifecycle state, so the proof itself cannot regrow into a state machine."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_legacy_import_model", "label": "LegacyImport Model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L180, L190", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepts only the spec FR-LEG-001 minimal format (source schema/hash, task identity, four materials, requirements, original facts) and rejects unknown, conflicting, corrupt or dual-write-demanding shapes; identical input yields identical identity."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_seven_behavior_facade", "label": "Seven-Behavior Public Runtime Facade", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L103-115, L186-189", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CLI stable behaviors are fixed at doctor/status/run/review/verify/confirm/authorize, shrinking the public cognitive surface while reusing TaskHandle and wh-review. The risk is a long-lived dual-track wrapper, so Phase 5 must delete the old entry points."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_writer_cutover", "label": "TaskHandle Atomic Writers and Writer Cutover", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L22, L176, L952-968", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TaskHandle keeps nofollow/create-only/CAS safety semantics; the cutover to the single new writer must be atomic, with the old writer remaining the only production writer until the full fault matrix (temp write, fsync, rename, CAS, current pointer) and concurrent single-winner idempotency are proven. If unprovable, the task STOPS rather than adding a sixth persistent object family."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_deletion_slices", "label": "Twelve Vertical Deletion Slices DEL-01..DEL-12", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L1058-1121", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each slice runs RED (prove the old entry is still reachable) then GREEN (delete grill replacement, phase trace lineage, dedicated invalidation, continuation, rebind, reopen, stage recovery, recovery/reset workspace CAS, duplicate projection, transition journal, shadow checkpoints, obsolete tools). A slice whose proof is incomplete or still has consumers is explicitly KEEP - KEEP is not failure and deleting to hit a count is forbidden; every GREEN keeps its own diff, evidence and revert boundary."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_delete_move_separation", "label": "DEC-003 Delete and Move Separation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L117-129", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tidy directories can mask mechanisms that still exist, so vertical deletion happens in Phase 5 and mechanical directory movement only in Phase 8; each behaviour change stays independently provable and revertible, and a KEEP slice does not block other proven slices."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_repository_inventory", "label": "Per-File Inventory and Deletion Plan Tools", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L853-892", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phase 0 generates a recomputable inventory, complexity baseline and deletion-proof contract before any production capability is removed; every tracked file must land in exactly one disposition and the 12 candidates must carry a proof status, with baseline numbers recomputed from the current tree rather than inherited from the downloaded plan."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_test_strategy", "label": "Test Strategy: 3 E2E, 5 Mutations, Writer Fault Matrix", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L840-847, L1162-1200", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three synthetic E2E scenarios (normal execution with unchanged Hub source, mid-task material revision plus severe-finding repair, idempotent resume after write interruption or unavailable review) plus five deliberate breakage samples (identity/tree/hash misbinding, missing completion, review unavailable or severe finding, confirmation-vs-authorization confusion, Bundle closure pollution) must all go red when the protection is broken. Behaviors are RED=1 on the behavior gate, paired GREEN=0, non-behavior gates=0, and mechanisms are deleted before their dedicated tests."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_three_provider_review", "label": "Final Three-Provider Architecture Review", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L1241-1279", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phase 9 runs clean install, the full quality matrix and a formal three-party architecture review through the official wh-review seam with providers fixed at kimi/k3, claude-code/opus and cursor/grok; if no aggregate semantic verdict forms, the canonical unavailable attempt and its diagnosis stay as audit facts and the verify summary states incomplete - never pass, never a fallback bridge, and historical provider trees are never work permits."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_human_gates", "label": "Two Human Gates T021 and T056", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L1286, L813", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "T021 confirms the planned deletion list before any irreversible removal and T056 confirms the actual deletions and diff at the end; commit, push, close and worktree deletion remain separately authorized, so plan confirmation can never be read as Git permission."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_clean_install_verification", "label": "Clean-Install Read-Only Runner Verification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L37, L1249-1261", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Business tasks run through a clean-install read-only Runner in a Mutica-like empty directory, and tracked plus untracked content hashes of the WorkflowHub source tree must be identical before and after, proving the Hub is never modified to work around the Hub."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_requirement_traceability", "label": "Requirement and Verification Traceability Matrix", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L1288-1337", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every FR maps to task IDs, AC IDs, phases and an owning gate/evidence, and the original dictated requirements plus the downloaded plan are audited so each item lands in spec, phase, task and an executable gate; the audit concludes that the downloaded plan's historical 30-day/one-release compatibility window is explicitly overridden by later dictation - no compatibility period, and unsafe handling is a STOP."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_document", "target": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_spec_document", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L5, L773", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_decision_log_full_inventory_governance", "target": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_repository_inventory", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L853-886", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_plan_requirement_traceability", "target": "specs_archive_workflowhub_complexity_governance_v2_spec_acceptance_criteria", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/plan.md", "source_location": "L1288-1307", "weig